  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Find all pairs of natural numbers $(m,n)$ for which $mn=4m+4n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(m,n)=(5,20),(6,12),(8,8),(12,6),(20,5)$.\n\nUse $(m-4)(n-4)=16$ and the positive factor pairs of $16$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}mn-4m-4n&=0\\\\n(m-4)-4(m-4)-16&=0\\\\(m-4)(n-4)&=16.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $mn=4m+4n>4m$ and $mn>4n$, both $m$ and $n$ exceed $4$. The ordered positive factor pairs of $16$ are $(1,16),(2,8),(4,4),(8,2),(16,1)$. Adding $4$ to each component gives\n\n$$(m,n)=(5,20),(6,12),(8,8),(12,6),(20,5).$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
